cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these results, please cite them as below."
title: "Backbite reconfiguration of Hamiltonian paths: the minimum-degree threshold is asymptotically n/2"
authors:
  - family-names: "Çam"
    given-names: "Efe"
version: "1.1"
date-released: "2026-11-26"
url: "https://github.com/the-arma-of-owl/kazazi-backbite-asymptotic"
repository-code: "https://github.com/the-arma-of-owl/kazazi-backbite-asymptotic"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
abstract: >-
  For every gamma > 0 and every sufficiently large n, every graph on n vertices
  with minimum degree at least (1/2 + gamma)n has a connected backbite
  reconfiguration graph R(G) of Hamiltonian paths. Together with Kazazi's
  constructions, the minimum-degree threshold in Kazazi's Conjecture 7.8
  (arXiv:2610.05068) is therefore n/2 + o(n). The repository also contains an
  exhaustive computer check of the conjecture for n <= 12, further
  computations, and two independent referee reports.
keywords:
  - graph theory
  - Hamiltonian paths
  - reconfiguration
  - backbite
  - Pósa rotation
  - minimum degree
